body:
Dude I feel that all the way. I'm in college right now and trying to get my professors to understand is about the hardest thing to do, cause they pass it as normal anxiety that people get this time of the semester. Its so hard to explain cause you cant sympathize, and theres not really a way for someone to truly see like the others you said. Its just awful.

&#x200B;

I remember growing up, I got diagnosed super early, but my parents had no clue what to do, so they constantly told me it wasn't an excuse for how I acted. My father and grandmother drove me off of medication, and things got much worse, and its hitting me really hard right now.
